    {
      "field": "runtime.py",
      "from": "byte-identical to the draft",
      "to": "draft runtime.py plus runtime-systemexit.patch",
      "why": "local v1 (plan 277bb9b2) failed: child() runs the frozen trainer with runpy.run_module inside scoped_loader, and the trainer ends with `raise SystemExit(main())`. A successful SFT probe (guard exit_code 0, 1 committed update) therefore raised SystemExit(0) through the context manager, the loader receipt recorded status failed / error_type SystemExit, and assert_probe stopped the run. The patch catches SystemExit around run_module only: code 0 or None leaves the block normally so the loader records completed; any other code is re-raised. aircraft_cpu_loader.py is pinned and shared with CI and is unchanged. verify-child calls builder.verify_submission(), which returns a report and never raises SystemExit, so it needs no change."
    },
    {
      "field": "name/local.root/local.probe_job/local.main_job/local.result",
      "from": "...-v2",
      "to": "...-v3",
      "why": "v1 and v2 outputs are preserved evidence of the failed attempts; v3 is a new single-use run"
    },
    {
      "field": "previous_attempt",
      "to": "{v1, v2}",
      "why": "pins the failed v1 and v2 plans, results and receipts, re-read by derive_plan.py"
    },
    {
      "field": "runtime.py STAGE_WALL_SECONDS[rl-exposure]",
      "from": 1800,
      "to": 4000,
      "why": "local v2 (plan a2cd71df): GRPO update 1 committed (752.76 s active, nonzero gradient) and after_train_diagnostic_predictions.json was written, then the 1800 s wall killed the stage at 1801.29 s inside the audit-only reload replay (exit -2). Projected need 1962.49 s (elapsed at kill + one after-train diagnostic; timing.json). 3600 s would be below 2x even the 1801.29 s lower bound, so the >= 2x rule gives 4000 s"
    },
    {
      "field": "runtime.py STAGE_WALL_SECONDS[sft-exposure]",
      "from": 1800,
      "to": 2000,
      "why": "same argv as the probe, which took 921.26 s in v2; 1800 s is 1.954x, short of the >= 2x rule"
    },
    {
      "field": "runtime.py STAGE_WALL_SECONDS[sft-resource-probe]",
      "from": 1800,
      "to": 2000,
      "why": "measured 921.26 s in v2; 1800 s is 1.954x, short of the >= 2x rule"
    },
    {
      "field": "runtime.py STAGE_WALL_SECONDS[sft-time] and the verify wall",
      "from": "3600 and 1800",
      "to": "unchanged",
      "why": "sft-time need 1592.07 s (probe fixed cost + RL active time; reaches 752.76 s in 10 of 32 steps), so 3600 s is >= 2x. Verify is unmeasured and bounded by the probe's start + model load + 8-row diagnostic (138.69 s), so 1800 s is >= 2x"
    },
    {
      "field": "prepare_task.py timeout_sec (Harbor task.toml [agent] timeout_sec)",
      "from": 7200,
      "to": 9900,
      "why": "the Harbor agent runs rl-exposure, sft-exposure and sft-time in series, with measured/projected need 4475.82 s, so 7200 s was below 2x; it must also enclose the new stage walls (4000 + 2000 + 3600) plus 300 s, or Harbor kills before the stage guard does"
    },
    {
      "field": "local.probe_wall_seconds/local.main_wall_seconds (local_run.py caps) and the README outer timeout",
      "from": "2100/9300/11700",
      "to": "2300/12000/14600",
      "why": "v2's construction (inner + 300 s) over the new inner walls: probe = probe stage wall + 300; main = agent timeout + verify wall + 300; outer = probe + main + 300. local_run.py require_wall_nesting refuses a plan that breaks this, and verify_bundle checks the packaged task.toml agent timeout"
    },
    {
      "field": "timing.json",
      "to": "added",
      "why": "per-phase timing of v2, re-measured by derive_plan.py from preserved evidence; derivation refuses if any wall is below 2x its need"
    },
